# URLs the link-rot guard is allowed to find missing in the current
# build. Format: one path per line; lines starting with `#` are ignored.
#
# An entry here is an explicit acknowledgement that a previously-published
# URL has been retired. Use sparingly — citation stability is one of the
# project's hard rules. When in doubt, redirect (`site/redirects.yaml`)
# instead of allowing.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixture → real-data transition (2026-04-23 / W17 first real run).
#
# The pre-launch fixture site rendered model pages for three providers
# (Opus, GPT-5-preview, Gemini 2.5 Pro). Real runs have never included
# Gemini and the model-week drill-downs (`/models/<x>/2026-W16/`) only
# render for the current week per build (see model_week.html). Those
# fixture-era URLs cannot be reproduced from real data.
#
# Going forward, the manifest_writer carries previously-seen models
# across weeks (see _enrich_models_with_history) so cadence-alternated
# providers (Opus on even weeks, GPT-5.1 on odd) keep rendering both
# /models/<x>/ pages every week and don't trip this guard.
/models/gemini-2.5-pro/
/models/gemini-2.5-pro/2026-W16/
/models/claude-opus-4-7/2026-W16/
# Retired here, and until 2026-08-15 also the target of a redirect from
# /models/gpt-5-preview/2026-W16/. That redirect served a 200 whose
# meta-refresh landed on this retired path, i.e. a hard 404, and the
# link-rot guard could not see it because it only diffed URL sets. The
# redirect now points at /models/gpt-5.1/, which is built every week,
# and scripts/check_linkrot.py resolves every redirect target against
# the new build. This line stays: the W16 drill-down itself is still
# retired.
/models/gpt-5.1/2026-W16/

# Temporarily missing on the W17→W18 transition: the W17 manifest
# (committed by the W17 pipeline run, before the carry-forward fix)
# does not list claude-opus-4-7. After the W18 run lands and the bot
# publishes the W18 manifest with carry-forward enabled, this URL
# reappears and the entry below becomes a harmless no-op. Leave it
# in place — removing it would re-break the URL during this single
# transition window.
/models/claude-opus-4-7/

